  "problem": "The helicopter's pilot wants to consider the effect of a linear transformation $T$ such that $T(r)=\u27e8-8,17,3\u27e9$ and $T(3q+r)=\u27e810,17,9\u27e9.$ Find the image of $q$ under the action of $T.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $T(q)=\\,\u27e8$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\u27e9.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(kq+hr)=T(kq)+T(hr)=kT(q)+hT(r)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor any vectors $q$ and $r.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3q+r) & =3T(q)+T(r) \\\\ \u27e810,17,9\u27e9 & =3T(q)+\u27e8-8,17,3\u27e9 \\\\ 3T(q) & =\u27e810,17,9\u27e9-\u27e8-8,17,3\u27e9 \\\\ 3T(q) & =\u27e818,0,6\u27e9 \\\\ T(q) & =\\frac{1}{3}\u27e818,0,6\u27e9 \\\\ T(q) & =\u27e86,0,2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
